[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2606272200-iriai-lifeline-commons-infra-funding-management", :adr/title "ADR-2606272200: iriai 入会 — global lifeline-commons (電気/水道/ガス/通信) infra + 資金 + 管理", :adr/status "accepted", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2606272200: iriai 入会 — global lifeline-commons (電気/水道/ガス/通信) infra + 資金 + 管理\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-06-27\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (founder, Council Lv7+ 1/1)\n\n# Context\n\nThe roster already has the four lifeline **producer** actors — 電気 **hikari 光** (ADR-2605261100),\n水道 **mizuho 水穂** (2605263100), ガス **kamado 竈** (2606051500), 通信 **noroshi 烽**\n(2606051600) — plus **infra-utility-connect** (the post-construction connection coordinator,\n2605250900), **kuni-umi** (the planetary-infra producer, 2605201400) and the **infra-robotics\n3-layer** runnable substrate (2606091800 / 2606101430). What was missing is the **non-profit\noperator of the lifelines *as one commons*** — the System-of-Systems umbrella that answers the\nquestion \"*who runs the shared electricity/water/gas/telecom business for everyone, non-profit?*\"\nacross **infra**, **資金 (funding)** and **管理 (management)** together.\n\nThat umbrella does not produce a lifeline (the producers do). Like **kaname 要** (2606172100) and\n**amime 網目** (2606212020) it is a **synthesizer**: it measures, per region × lifeline, who lacks\nan essential lifeline (the **§1.16 social-security reach gap**) and where the network is fragile\n(single-source SPOF / N-1 contingency), then routes each cell to a commons action — and wires that\naction onto the **existing non-profit funding rails** and the **existing 1 SBT = 1 vote governance**.\n\n**入会 (iriai)** is the precise frame: the traditional Japanese **commons** — collectively-held\nrights of use over a shared resource (forest/water/pasture). The four lifelines (ライフライン)\nare held as a commons right of use (**入会権**), the charter-clean inversion of both the for-profit\nutility (Veolia/Suez/utility-PE) and of **utility-as-coercion** (a lifeline withheld as leverage).\n\n# Decision\n\nIntroduce **iriai 入会** — a clj-native Tier-B actor (`20-actors/iriai/`,\n`did:web:etzhayyim.com:iriai`, `com.etzhayyim.iriai.*`). It is **ASSESSMENT + R0 DESIGN ONLY**:\nit never produces and never actuates a lifeline; it MAPS, PROPOSES funding, and ENVELOPES\ngovernance. Three layers, one heartbeat.\n\n## 1. infra — System-of-Systems coverage + resilience (`methods/infra.cljc`)\n\nPer region × lifeline cell, **edge-primary on read**:\n\n```\ncoverage    = served-pop / total-pop\ncommons-gap = (1 − coverage) · essentiality[lifeline] · (0.5 + 0.5·vulnerability)\n```\n\nDisclosed **life-first essentiality**: 水 1.0 · 電 0.9 · 通信 0.7 · ガス 0.6. Resilience =\n`single-source?` (SPOF) + `n1-margin` (N-1 contingency; < 0 = chokepoint, the amime lens).\n\n**verdict ∈ {:await-consent :provision :reinforce :redundancy :maintain :monitor}**, in order —\nconsent gates every *build*, but a lifeline is never *withheld* (there is no deny route):\n\n1. action-needed AND consent absent → **:await-consent** (land/community sovereignty, ADR-2605192245)\n2. disaster-degraded → **:reinforce** (restore to baseline, not greenfield)\n3. commons-gap ≥ 0.30 → **:provision** (close the §1.16 reach gap)\n4. single-source OR N-1 < 0 → **:redundancy** (no SPOF for a lifeline)\n5. coverage ≥ 0.85 AND resilient → **:maintain**\n6. else → **:monitor**\n\nA **coverage + resilience MAP**, never a target-list, **never a shut-off list** (G1). `:source`\nnames the producer actor (電気→hikari · 水道→mizuho · ガス→kamado · 通信→noroshi); iriai composes,\nnever produces.\n\n## 2. 資金 (funding) — §1.16 social-security IN-KIND (`methods/fund.cljc`)\n\nEach `:provision`/`:reinforce`/`:redundancy` cell becomes a charter-clean **funding proposal** on\nthe **existing non-profit rails** — the **subaru 昴** in-kind precedent (2606162355) + the\n**tanemaki 種蒔き** give-only steward pattern (2606122001) pointed at the lifelines:\n\n```\ndonation (USDC/Base/ERC-4337, or non-custodial fiat→USDC on-ramp, ADR-2606111800)\n  → TitheRouter 10% auto-split → Public Fund\n  → grant / milestone-escrow / in-kind   (decided by 1 SBT = 1 vote, NOT by iriai)\n  → producer actor builds + operates\n  → delivery is §1.16 SOCIAL-SECURITY IN-KIND (covenantal-universal): cash ≡ 0 to the consumer\n  + Displacement-Dividend coupling (ADR-2606032130): build/ops labour freed by OSS robotics\n    funds a tenure-weighted in-kind cohort pool (no live displacement without a funded cohort)\n```\n\n**Imputed value** (market-equivalent annual worth of the in-kind delivery, aggregate,\nmethod-versioned, transparency-only per ADR-2605301020) proves the §1.16 income is **HIGH** while\n**cash ≡ 0** — it is **not a price and not a bill** (G2). Instruments are **{:grant :milestone-escrow\n:in-kind}** only; equity/debt/revenue-share/subscription/tariff are **unrepresentable**. Every\nproposal is `advisory:true / binds-fund:false / decided-by 1-sbt-1-vote` — iriai is a **steward,\nnot a sovereign** (G3).\n\n## 3. 管理 (management) — 1 SBT = 1 vote governance + Transparent-Force discipline (`methods/manage.cljc`)\n\nEach proposal is wrapped in the governance + actuation + accountability envelope:\n\n- **Governance route** — 1 SBT = 1 vote (PublicFundGovernance: 20% quorum / 50% of cast / 7-day\n  vote / 48h timelock) + Council attestation (= PR review in bootstrap). Critical-infra\n  (electric/water) provision escalates to **Council Lv7+** (Transparent-Force §1.12).\n- **Actuation class** — **compute-only R0**: iriai stops at **:intent**. The live act (energize a\n  grid / open a valve / ignite gas / activate a link) is the producer actor's cell under\n  **Council Lv7+ + operator-DID + member signature** — the infra-robotics R0 precedent\n  (2606091800/2606101430, where `cell.solve()` stays gated, dry-run only). `:iriai/actuate` is\n  unrepresentable (G5).\n- **Accountability** — **no-server-key** (2605231525): iriai holds no key; autonomous writes are\n  attributed to a consenting member via a **CACAO leash** (ibuki/kaname/tsubasa, 2606111400);\n  every decision is on-chain-logged + open-source (§1.12).\n\n## Persistence + heartbeat\n\nState is the **kotoba Datom log** (2605262130 / 2605312345): the deterministic, idempotent-by-content\nheartbeat (`methods/autorun.cljc`) folds infra+fund+manage into one content-addressed transaction\nappended to an append-only tamper-evident commit-DAG (`methods/kotoba.cljc`, verify-chain), the\nkafun/ugachi/busshi family machinery. An unchanged beat is a no-op. No-server-key, no network I/O.\n\n## Gates (constitutional; the charter inversions, structurally enforced — `methods/gates.cljc`)\n\n- **G1 commons-map-not-shutoff-list** — a lifeline is a commons right, never withheld;\n  `:iriai/shutoff` / `:iriai/disconnect` / `:iriai.region/deny` / `:iriai.person/*` unrepresentable.\n- **G2 commons-not-a-market** — cash ≡ 0; never billed/disconnected-for-nonpayment; give-only\n  instruments; `:iriai.fund/tariff|price|subscription|equity` unrepresentable.\n- **G3 steward-not-sovereign** — no `:iriai/fund` / `:iriai.manage/decide`; advisory + 1 SBT=1 vote.\n- **G4 non-profit-rails-only** — donation → tithe → Public Fund; no custodial-fiat / ad / for-profit capture.\n- **G5 assessment-r0-only-never-acts** — `:intent` only; `:iriai/actuate` unrepresentable.\n- **G6 no-server-key** — keyless; member-CACAO attribution; local-only heartbeat.\n- **G7 kotoba-eavt-native** · **G8 synthetic-seed**.\n\nThe strongest gates are **structural**: the forbidden acts have no attribute to express them, and\n`gates/forbidden-absent?` proves the whole emitted datom stream never contains one (test-enforced).\n\n# Consequences\n\n- **R0 landed**: `20-actors/iriai/` — 7 methods + 6 test suites (**40 tests / 311 assertions green**,\n  bb), ontology + negative-space, 6-region × 4-lifeline synthetic seed spanning all six verdicts,\n  append-only commons ledger (514 datoms on the seed beat, chain verifies), manifest + docs.\n- The four producer actors now have a **non-profit SoS operator** that funds (§1.16 in-kind, cash≡0)\n  and governs (1 SBT=1 vote) their deployment — the lifeline answer to the §1.16 social-security\n  mission, on the subaru in-kind precedent.\n- **Compute-only / no-actuation** keeps the Transparent-Force §1.12 boundary intact: iriai decisions\n  stop at `:intent`; production + live actuation stay the producer actors' under Council Lv7+.\n- **R1+ (G7-gated)**: real region/utility-coverage ingest from public open data (World Bank / IEA /\n  WHO-JMP / ITU — read-only, no key, the \"no-server-key bars a custodial key, not read-only public\n  ingest\" clarification); inochi/jinushi land-sovereignty grounding for consent; amime N-1 energy-mesh\n  join for the electric layer; fleet registration (cell-runner + healthz); live kotoba-engine bridge;\n  lexicon JSON. Live actuation stays the producer actors' under Council Lv7+, never iriai.\n\n# Alternatives Considered\n\n- **Extend infra-utility-connect instead of a new actor.** Rejected: infra-utility-connect is the\n  narrow *post-construction connection coordinator* (4-cell Pregel handoff); the SoS coverage +\n  funding + governance umbrella is a distinct concern and a distinct altitude (it *composes*\n  infra-utility-connect, the way kaname composes the mirrors).\n- **Fold funding + governance into each producer actor.** Rejected: that would duplicate the\n  §1.16-in-kind + 1-SBT-1-vote logic four times and lose the cross-lifeline commons view (a region\n  unserved on *all four* lifelines is one reach-gap, not four).\n- **A market/metered design with subsidized tariffs.** Rejected on charter grounds: a lifeline is a\n  commons right (入会権), delivered §1.16 in-kind (cash≡0); tariff/subscription/disconnect are\n  unrepresentable (G2) — the inversion of utility-as-coercion.\n\n# References\n\n- `20-actors/iriai/` — manifest, methods (infra/fund/manage/gates/kotoba/autorun), seed, ontology, tests\n- `20-actors/iriai/CLAUDE.md` — actor docstring\n- Producer actors: hikari (2605261100) · mizuho (2605263100) · kamado (2606051500) · noroshi (2606051600)\n- Funding doctrine: 2605301020 (BHI) · 2605302357 (§1.16) · 2606032130 (Displacement Dividend) ·\n  2606162355 (subaru in-kind precedent) · 2606122001 (tanemaki steward) · 2606111800 (donation media)\n- Governance: 2605192100 §1.12/§1.16 · 2605231525 (no-server-key) · 2606111400 (CACAO leash)\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2606272200-iriai-lifeline-commons-infra-funding-management.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "iriai-lifeline-commons", :adr/last_verified "2026-06-27", :adr/date "2026-06-27", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/related ["2605250900  # infra-utility-connect (connection coordinator)" "2605261100  # hikari 光 (electric)" "2605263100  # mizuho 水穂 (water)" "2606051500  # kamado 竈 (gas)" "2606051600  # noroshi 烽 (telecom)" "2605201400  # kuni-umi (planetary-infra producer)" "2606091800  # infra-robotics 3-layer operational substrate" "2606101430  # infra-robotics R1 device-in-the-loop" "2606162355  # torifune/subaru — §1.16 in-kind connectivity-commons precedent" "2606122001  # tanemaki — Public Fund grant-steward (give-only, steward-not-sovereign)" "2606052300  # fuchi — in-kind sustenance allocator (cash≡0)" "2606032130  # Displacement Dividend (tenure-weighted in-kind)" "2605301020  # Basic High Income (imputed-income + commons-asset)" "2605302357  # Social Security for Humanity §1.16" "2606012100  # donation-funded operation + in-kind compute donation" "2606111800  # donation media expansion (fiat in-kind + non-custodial on-ramp)" "2605192245  # global land sovereignty (waqf-equivalent inalienability)" "2606111400  # revocable CACAO member-delegation leash" "2606212020  # amime energy-mesh (N-1 contingency)" "2606172100  # kaname SoS synthesizer (pattern)"], :adr/authoritative_for ["iriai-lifeline-commons" "lifeline-commons-funding-§1.16-in-kind" "lifeline-commons-governance-1sbt1vote"]}]
